 "notes": [
  "CMP citywide averages are network travel-time-weighted (total segment length / total travel time). Recomputed from the API for 2024 this reproduces the report exactly (16.85/15.75 arterial, 33.92/25.06 freeway); for 2025 the API gives 16.22/14.77 and 31.44/22.99, a little off the report's 16.1/14.7/32.7/23.9 (segment set may differ slightly).",
  "Corridor speeds below are computed here the same way (sum of length / sum of length/speed over that corridor's CMP segments in one direction) from the 2025 per-segment values in the API, which match the report's Fig 4-4 segment CSV.",
  "muniTransitAM/PM on corridors = CMP 2025 Muni transit speed on those segments (APC/AVL), where reported.",
  "Freeway segments are I-80, I-280 and US-101 only; 19th Ave/Park Presidio is classed arterial though its Lake-US-101 tunnel segments run ~40-45 mph.",
  "Speeds are INRIX probe speeds (mostly passenger cars), including signal delay.",
  "Corridor 'from'/'to' are the chain ends of that direction's CMP segments with 2025 data (a corridor direction may have a gap, e.g. Fell/Oak are one-way pairs with short counter-flow segments). Where 2024 lacked some segments, 2024 vs 2025 is given on the common segment set only."
 ],
